HST Office: rotating HASON TECH solution banner in the ribbon of HST Writer, Sheets and Slides.

Owner decisions (2026-11-04): one banner set for all apps, rotating every rotateSeconds (default 10);
users cannot hide it and there is no administrator switch; a click opens the item's URL with UTM in
the system browser. Content only comes from the data layer of the bundled extension
(docs/BANNERS.md: installed defaults, verified cache, signed system.hasontech.vn feed).

- sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstRibbonBanner.{hxx,cxx} (new): a VCL control drawn at the right end of
  the Tabbed notebookbar (notebookbar.ui) of Writer, Calc and Impress, beside the 2-row groups.
  The slot adapts to the ribbon, never the other way round: its height is the height of the tab
  page that already holds the groups, its width keeps the 360:104 ratio of the artwork and is
  capped at 360 logical px. The ribbon height and the group heights do not change. Images of any
  pixel size are aspect-fitted with a high-quality downscale from the matching @1x/@2x/@3x variant
  (device pixels: VCL DPI factor x cairo surface scale on gtk, 2 on macOS).
  Data: org.hst.office.BannerFeed (XJob, Scale/Slot -> JSON) is called on a worker thread; results
  are posted to the main thread. Before the first result, and whenever the service is missing or
  fails, the installed defaults are read directly from the bundled extension
  ($BRAND_BASE_DIR/share/extensions/hst-vietnamese-tools/data/banners.json, banners/*.png, UTM
  from data/solutions.json), so the slot is never empty and startup never waits for Python.
  Rotation: a main-thread timer requests Slot+1; paused while hovered or focused; a 300 ms
  cross-fade, or a plain switch when animations are reduced (Accessibility option / OS setting).
  Keyboard focusable (focus ring), accessible role HYPER_LINK, accessible name and tooltip
  "<name> — <tagline>"; Enter, Space or a click opens the URL with com.sun.star.system.SystemShellExecute,
  without any error dialog; a worker asks the service for the destination first (click counter
  down: the home page). Double clicks open one tab. In dark mode the light artwork sits on a light
  rounded card. Decoder errors skip to the next entry without disturbing editing.
- sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstBannerGeometry.hxx (new): slot, fit and variant arithmetic without
  LibreOffice types (unit test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_banner_geometry.py).
- sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx, sfx2/inc/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.hxx:
  creates the banner for modules/{swriter,scalc,simpress}/ui/notebookbar.ui only, narrows the
  current tab page by the slot (the groups fold into their overflow menu as before) and restores
  the full width when the window is narrower than 1280 logical px. Narrowing runs after the tab
  control's own page allocation has finished (posted user event): done inside it, the allocation
  continued with the full width and moved the Impress groups 4 px down.
- sfx2/Library_sfx.mk: the new source file.
- vcl/source/window/accessibility.cxx: the notebookbar sits in the border window and was unreachable for
  assistive technology; it is now reported as a child of THE workwindow, like the menubar.
- vcl/source/accessibility/vclxaccessibletabcontrol.cxx: a visible link child placed on a tab control (the
  banner) follows the page tabs in the accessible children.

The control is plain VCL with no backend-specific code besides the HiDPI scale query.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files are MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/runtime/check-ribbon-banner.py (gtk3, Writer/Sheets/Slides), tests/unit/test_ribbon_banner_geometry.py.
